<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bardas Phokas the Younger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 940–<a href="/years/989">989</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Bardas Phocas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barda">Bardas</a> Phokas the Younger was a Byzantine general of the Phokas family who took part in three revolts for and against the ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-dynasty">Macedonian dynasty</a>. A nephew of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-i">Emperor Nikephoros</a> II Phokas, he was proclaimed emperor by troops at Caesarea after his uncle's death in 969, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bardas-skleros">Bardas Skleros</a> put the revolt down and he spent seven years in exile on Chios. Freed in 978 to fight Skleros, who had himself rebelled, he defeated him with the help of a Georgian army and in single combat, and became Domestic of the Scholae. In 987 he rebelled again and overran most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>, but facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a> at Abydos in 989 he suffered a seizure and fell dead from his horse.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Byzantine general <b>Bardas Phokas the Younger</b> died in the battle of Abydos, on the Hellespont, ending his second rebellion against Emperor Basil II.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-13">13 April in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Cappadocia. Died in Abydos, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=40.2,26.41&amp;year=971" aria-label="Abydos on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5199 726 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Bardas Phokas the Younger"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5649 996h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5649 996h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=40.2,26.41&amp;year=971">What was here in 971 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
